{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.DirectionalWronskian","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.DirectionalWronskian","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.GenWronskian","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.LineRestriction","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.CharZero.Infinite"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.dirGenWronskian_ne_zero_iff_exists_linearIndependent_lineRestrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.dirGenWronskian_ne_zero_iff_exists_linearIndependent_lineRestrict","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/DirectionalWronskian.lean#L122-L133","doc":"**The directional Wronskian is non-zero exactly when some line in that direction has\nindependent restrictions.**\n\nThe base point drops out of the problem: what is left to decide is a question about the\n**direction alone**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_linearIndependent_lineRestrict_of_dirGenWronskian_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_linearIndependent_lineRestrict_of_dirGenWronskian_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/DirectionalWronskian.lean#L104-L120","doc":"Conversely, a non-zero directional Wronskian produces a line whose restrictions are\nindependent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.dirGenWronskian_ne_zero_of_lineRestrict_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.dirGenWronskian_ne_zero_of_lineRestrict_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/DirectionalWronskian.lean#L88-L102","doc":"Independent restrictions force a non-zero directional Wronskian: the univariate\ncriterion, which already carries the order bound, transfers upstairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.lineRestrict_dirGenWronskian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.lineRestrict_dirGenWronskian","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/DirectionalWronskian.lean#L65-L82","doc":"**The pullback:** restricting the directional Wronskian to a line gives the ordinary\nunivariate Wronskian of the restrictions.\n\n`lineRestrict` is an `AlgHom`, so it commutes with `det`; the entries then match by the\niterated chain rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.dirGenWronskian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.dirGenWronskian","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/DirectionalWronskian.lean#L57-L63","doc":"The **directional generalized Wronskian**: `det ((Dᶜ)ⁱ fⱼ)`.\n\nIts rows have order `0, 1, …, m-1` by construction, which is exactly the bound Roth's lemma\nasks for — the bound is inherited from `Dᶜ` rather than engineered. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.dirWronskianMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.dirWronskianMatrix","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/DirectionalWronskian.lean#L52-L55","doc":"The Wronskian matrix built from the directional derivative `Dᶜ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}